    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0585" n="465" xml:id="pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/905</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Peruvian Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Prada</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to the Chargé d’Affaires ad
                    interim of Peru, and has the honor to acknowledge the receipt of his note of
                    April 30, 1922,<anchor n="6" xml:id="d213-f1"/> to the effect that the delegates
                    who will represent the Government of Peru at the Conference to be held with the
                    delegates of the Chilean Government, are to arrive in this city in the near
                    future, and that no objection is perceived on the part of the Peruvian
                    delegation to opening this Conference on the 12th of May next.</p>
                <p>This information will be transmitted to the Chilean Embassy in Washington, with a
                    view to fixing May 12th as the date for the opening of the Conference.<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d213-f2"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1922-05-04"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">May 4, 1922</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d213-f1" n="6" xml:id="d213-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d213-f2" n="7" xml:id="d213-f2-content">
                <p>This date was accepted by the Chilean Ambassador, but was later changed to May 15
                    by agreement between the Chilean and Peruvian Ambassadors.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
